        "body": "This migrates the selected Learned Intelligence numerical core into `devtools.learning` and adds a bounded learning investigator composed through Devtools ModelInteraction, native Tools, ToolRunner and trusted host admission. A parent can submit an admitted objective, receive an independently inspected fitted artifact, and make actual label-free predictions.\n\nThe supported first capability includes binary kNN7/SQUARE logistic/margin and regression Mean/Ridge/kNN-v2, training-only preparation, F1/MAE observations and typed nonvalues, retained fitted states, immutable scientific publication and independent numerical/source inspection. Proposals do not confer authority: source/role/method/evidence/budget checks precede exact caller grants. Acknowledged observations precede subsequent decisions; protected final evaluation follows terminal selection. STOP, CONTINUE and ABSTAIN are exercised through scripted ModelInteraction without live inference or automatic retry of uncertain effects.\n\nExisting Commands/Resources own suspended-start Windows Job custody, assignment before execution, one-process/native-thread bounds, timeout, cancellation and descendant cleanup. Ordinary base installation remains free of mandatory numerical libraries. Histogram, residual composition, ranking, clustering, association, historical failed policies and research archives remain outside the installed capability.\n\nDonor provenance is pinned to `e069092e9b83c349ddb4efee09a3b1891ea0ad63`, with exact selected-source mappings and adaptations in `docs/development/learning-migration-provenance.json`. Original Iris and Auto MPG engineering evidence is preserved: final Iris F1 1.0, MPG kNN-v2 MAE 2.8101694915254236, with actual parent consumption. These exposed development fixtures establish engineering behavior, not strategy effectiveness or generalization.\n\nMain reconciliation uses normal merge `c66961a32d138fcbff95f2841765a3e6491238ef`, integrating `825bc23b98e366e97d56e3146a1d752285f383bd` into feature `cbe8804812abf60a530b5aceed93c64edd577605`. The documentation map merged automatically; no manual conflict or contract change was needed. Reviewer enrollment stays separate from scientific grants. Main's bounded llama.cpp transport fixes are retained. Canonical main and model services were not modified by this assignment.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Combined protected development gate: 5,275 passed, two existing optional skips; 100% of 19,325 statements and 5,246 branches on committed `c66961a32d138fcbff95f2841765a3e6491238ef`; stable inputs.\n- Affected compatibility tests: 2,078 passed, two existing optional skips; stable inputs.\n- Maintained Ruff, formatting (923 files), strict mypy (768 modules), layout and diff checks pass.\n- Rebuilt installed wheel SHA-256 `81a384dbb16f507710f617739fe9523ec7a47cea33cc43f9d50cb07cf585a8a7`: all 409 packaged source members and all three installed copies authenticated. Base coding/repository operation and six real numerical/Tool controls pass with donor, development source, canonical checkout and archives denied.\n- Qualified numerical worker: Windows x64 CPython 3.12.13, NumPy 2.5.3, SciPy 1.18.1, scikit-learn 1.9.1, threadpoolctl 3.7.0; observed native pools one thread. CPython 3.14.3 host without numerical dependencies successfully uses the existing explicit constructor to invoke that separately installed 3.12 worker, including both families, inspection, refusals and parent predictions. This is not qualification of native scientific fitting under Python 3.14.\n- Four installed Python 3.14 host / direct Python 3.12 child custody controls pass: actual descendant refusal, timeout, cancellation after entry, and suspended-child cleanup following explicitly simulated admission refusal, with exact PID/return-code and marker evidence.\n- Read-only reinspection through the combined installed wheel under both Python 3.12 and numerical-free Python 3.14 hosts accepts all seven original protocol-v2 publications and still refuses all seven protocol-v1 publications; both 80-member sets remain unchanged. All original observations and prediction sequences match across hosts, including the 34 Iris and 59 MPG protected final predictions. No original scientific study was repeated.\n\nSee `docs/development/learning-main-reconciliation.md` and the linked raw receipts for final producing revisions, runtime identities, costs and limitations. Peak process-tree memory, energy and generalization are not measured. No reviewer approval, CI result or human acceptance is claimed. The next milestone is live locally hosted hypothesis generation from genuine task evidence against strong deterministic references; it is outside this PR's executed qualification. This PR is for human integration review; it must not be merged automatically.\n",
